      "side": 0,
      "message": "I think this is the right understanding of removing these reads. Let me know if you had something else in mind.\n\nIn the current code, we reread the registers prior to scheduling the deferred handler. That means that the only bits observed on line 576 would be ones that were reasserted after being read on line 561 (presumably due to not being fully handled). When the deferred function was scheduled, it would reread the registers to see if anything still needed to be handled (had been reasserted between syv682x_handle_interrupt calls). To finish the process, each register was read 2-4 times over 1-2 handler calls, assuming nothing else happened.\n\nIn the new code, we re-read the registers during the deferred handler call, getting the bits that reasserted after the read in the previous handler call. Each register is read 2 times over 2 handler calls.\n\nThis means we\u0027ll almost certainly go through one cycle of deferred call but reduce the overall number of reads.",
